  "body": "Should the `rel` attribute be valid on the `iframe` element? The [purpose of `rel`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Attributes/rel) is to describe the relation of a **linked resource** to the current document. The `iframe` element is **essentially a link** that happens to be rendered within its parent document, thus it seems reasonable that it should support the `rel` attribute.\r\n\r\nCurrently [`rel` is only valid](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#introduction-2) on `link`, `a`, `area`, and `form`.\r\n\r\nFor context, in a REST API, I'd like to use a custom link relation on an `iframe` to indicate to the client what type of resource is being referenced by the `iframe`.",
